{"id":"mahabharata-12-251","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":251,"title":"एकपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 251 · What dharma is","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira says that men doubt dharma and asks what it is and where it comes from. Bhishma answers that the man who has done nothing wrong is unafraid, going without fear to the king's gate, and gives the marks of dharma.","kn":"ಜನರು ಧರ್ಮದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಸಂಶಯಪಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಧರ್ಮವೆಂದರೇನು, ಎಲ್ಲಿಂದ ಬರುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಪ್ಪು ಮಾಡದವನು ಭಯವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ರಾಜದ್ವಾರಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಧರ್ಮದ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि लोग धर्म पर शंका करते हैं और पूछते हैं कि धर्म क्या है और कहाँ से आता है। भीष्म उत्तर देते हैं कि जिसने कुछ बुरा नहीं किया वह निर्भय होकर राजद्वार जाता है, और धर्म के लक्षण बताते हैं।","te":"ప్రజలు ధర్మంపై సందేహపడుతున్నారని, ధర్మం అంటే ఏమిటి, ఎక్కడి నుండి వస్తుందని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. తప్పు చేయనివాడు భయం లేకుండా రాజద్వారం వెళ్తాడని చెప్పి భీష్ముడు ధర్మ లక్షణాలను ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"மக்கள் தர்மத்தில் ஐயம் கொள்கின்றனர், தர்மம் என்றால் என்ன, எங்கிருந்து வருகிறது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்கிறார். தவறு செய்யாதவன் அச்சமின்றி அரசவாயிலுக்குச் செல்வான் என்று கூறிப் பீஷ்மர் தர்மத்தின் அடையாளங்களைத் தருகிறார்.","ml":"മനുഷ്യർ ധർമ്മത്തിൽ സംശയിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു; ധർമ്മമെന്തെന്നും അത് എവിടെനിന്ന് വരുന്നുവെന്നും ചോദിക്കുന്നു. തെറ്റൊന്നും ചെയ്യാത്തവൻ ഭയമില്ലാതെ രാജാവിന്റെ കവാടത്തിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നുവെന്നും, ധർമ്മത്തിന്റെ ലക്ഷണങ്ങൾ ഇതൊക്കെയാണെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.251; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इमे वै मानवाः सर्वे धर्मं प्रति विशङ्किताः ।\nकोऽयं धर्मः कुतो धर्मस्तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these people are in doubt about dharma. What is this dharma and where does it come from? Tell me, grandfather."}},{"n":2,"text":"धर्मो न्वयमिहार्थः किममुत्रार्थोऽपि वा भवेत् ।\nउभयार्थोऽपि वा धर्मस्तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is this dharma for the sake of this world, or for the next, or for both? Tell me that, grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"सदाचारः स्मृतिर्वेदास्त्रिविधं धर्मलक्षणम् ।\nचतुर्थमर्थमित्याहुः कवयो धर्मलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good conduct, tradition and the Vedas are the threefold mark of dharma; the wise call the fourth, purpose, also a mark of dharma."}},{"n":4,"text":"अपि ह्युक्तानि कर्माणि व्यवस्यन्त्युत्तरावरे ।\nलोकयात्रार्थमेवेह धर्मस्य नियमः कृतः ।\nउभयत्र सुखोदर्क इह चैव परत्र च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the prescribed acts decide the higher and the lower; the rule of dharma is made only for the conduct of the world, and it brings happy results both here and hereafter."}},{"n":5,"text":"अलब्ध्वा निपुणं धर्मं पापः पापे प्रसज्जति ।\nन च पापकृतः पापान्मुच्यन्ते केचिदापदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without finding subtle dharma, the sinner clings to sin, and none who do sin are freed from it in calamity."}},{"n":6,"text":"अपापवादी भवति यदा भवति धर्मवित् ।\nधर्मस्य निष्ठा स्वाचारस्तमेवाश्रित्य भोत्स्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"One becomes free of blame when he becomes a knower of dharma; the foundation of dharma is one's own conduct, and relying on it you will understand."}},{"n":7,"text":"यदाधर्मसमाविष्टो धनं गृह्णाति तस्करः ।\nरमते निर्हरन्स्तेनः परवित्तमराजके ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a thief, filled with adharma, takes wealth, he enjoys himself, carrying off others' goods where there is no king."}},{"n":8,"text":"यदास्य तद्धरन्त्यन्ये तदा राजानमिच्छति ।\nतदा तेषां स्पृहयते ये वै तुष्टाः स्वकैर्धनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When others take his own, then he wants a king, and then he envies those who are content with their own wealth."}},{"n":9,"text":"अभीतः शुचिरभ्येति राजद्वारमशङ्कितः ।\nन हि दुश्चरितं किंचिदन्तरात्मनि पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pure man goes to the king's door fearless and unsuspecting, for he sees no ill deed in his heart."}},{"n":10,"text":"सत्यस्य वचनं साधु न सत्याद्विद्यते परम् ।\nसत्येन विधृतं सर्वं सर्वं सत्ये प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speaking truth is good, and there is nothing higher than truth; by truth all is upheld, and all rests in truth."}},{"n":11,"text":"अपि पापकृतो रौद्राः सत्यं कृत्वा पृथक्पृथक् ।\nअद्रोहमविसंवादं प्रवर्तन्ते तदाश्रयाः ।\nते चेन्मिथोऽधृतिं कुर्युर्विनश्येयुरसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even terrible sinners, having each made a promise of truth, act without treachery or deceit, relying on it; if they made each other uneasy, they would surely perish."}},{"n":12,"text":"न हर्तव्यं परधनमिति धर्मः सनातनः ।\nमन्यन्ते बलवन्तस्तं दुर्बलैः संप्रवर्तितम् ।\nयदा नियतिदौर्बल्यमथैषामेव रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Another's wealth must not be taken\" is eternal dharma. The strong think it was set up by the weak, until fate makes weakness fall to themselves."}},{"n":13,"text":"न ह्यत्यन्तं बलयुता भवन्ति सुखिनोऽपि वा ।\nतस्मादनार्जवे बुद्धिर्न कार्या ते कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have great strength are not extremely strong or happy for ever; so you should never set your mind on crookedness."}},{"n":14,"text":"असाधुभ्योऽस्य न भयं न चोरेभ्यो न राजतः ।\nन किंचित्कस्यचित्कुर्वन्निर्भयः शुचिरावसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The honest man has no fear from the wicked, from thieves, or from the king; doing nothing to anyone, he lives fearless and pure."}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वतः शङ्कते स्तेनो मृगो ग्राममिवेयिवान् ।\nबहुधाचरितं पापमन्यत्रैवानुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thief suspects everyone on every side, like a deer that has entered a village; he sees the sins he has done many times elsewhere."}},{"n":16,"text":"मुदितः शुचिरभ्येति सर्वतो निर्भयः सदा ।\nन हि दुश्चरितं किंचिदात्मनोऽन्येषु पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cheerful and pure man goes everywhere, always fearless, for he sees no ill deed of his own in others."}},{"n":17,"text":"दातव्यमित्ययं धर्म उक्तो भूतहिते रतैः ।\nतं मन्यन्ते धनयुताः कृपणैः संप्रवर्तितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It must be given\" is a dharma spoken by those devoted to the good of beings; the wealthy think it was set up by the miserly,"}},{"n":18,"text":"यदा नियतिकार्पण्यमथैषामेव रोचते ।\nन ह्यत्यन्तं धनवन्तो भवन्ति सुखिनोऽपि वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"until fate's meanness falls on themselves; for the rich too are not extremely happy."}},{"n":19,"text":"यदन्यैर्विहितं नेच्छेदात्मनः कर्म पूरुषः ।\nन तत्परेषु कुर्वीत जानन्नप्रियमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What a man would not wish others to do to him, he should not do to others, knowing it to be unpleasant to himself."}},{"n":20,"text":"योऽन्यस्य स्यादुपपतिः स कं किं वक्तुमर्हति ।\nयदन्यस्तस्य तत्कुर्यान्न मृष्येदिति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is another's lover, what can he say to anyone? My view is that he would not tolerate what another does to him."}},{"n":21,"text":"जीवितुं यः स्वयं चेच्छेत्कथं सोऽन्यं प्रघातयेत् ।\nयद्यदात्मन इच्छेत तत्परस्यापि चिन्तयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can he who wants to live himself have another killed? Whatever he wishes for himself, he should think of for others also."}},{"n":22,"text":"अतिरिक्तैः संविभजेद्भोगैरन्यानकिंचनान् ।\nएतस्मात्कारणाद्धात्रा कुसीदं संप्रवर्तितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should share his surplus enjoyments with the poor; for this reason the Creator set up lending at interest."}},{"n":23,"text":"यस्मिंस्तु देवाः समये संतिष्ठेरंस्तथा भवेत् ।\nअथ चेल्लाभसमये स्थितिर्धर्मेऽपि शोभना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the gods would stand firm in an agreement, so it should be; and if there is a fair rule even in dharma at the time of gain,"}},{"n":24,"text":"सर्वं प्रियाभ्युपगतं धर्ममाहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nपश्यैतं लक्षणोद्देशं धर्माधर्मे युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"the wise say dharma is whatever is accepted as dear to all. See this mark, Yudhishthira, of dharma and adharma."}},{"n":25,"text":"लोकसंग्रहसंयुक्तं विधात्रा विहितं पुरा ।\nसूक्ष्मधर्मार्थनियतं सतां चरितमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was laid down by the Maker long ago, joined with the maintenance of the world; the best conduct of the good is bound to subtle dharma and purpose."}},{"n":26,"text":"धर्मलक्षणमाख्यातमेतत्ते कुरुसत्तम ।\nतस्मादनार्जवे बुद्धिर्न कार्या ते कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you the mark of dharma, best of Kurus; therefore you should never set your mind on crookedness."}}]}]}